gc exits `fatal error: all goroutines are asleep - deadlock!` once
every goroutine is parked with no possible wake (here: main's second
recv, the sender already gone). minigo previously parked forever;
it now fails the same way — the proc deadlock watch declares the
fatal and the CLI reports `minigo: fatal error: ...`. This record
stays PENDING because want.stdout cannot express an expected fatal:
to the harness the outcome is a runErr either way (same class as the
trap records in mapkey_namedstruct / ptrconv_ptrptr).
